   "render_note_id": "cite_note-16",
   "marker": "none",
   "marker_text": "Writing in 1942, Edward Warren argued that in 1168 Henry II summoned Reginald as a serjeant-at-law,[13] but later researchers have not agreed with Warren's conclusions.[1][14] According to Warren, the others summoned by Henry were: 1174: John de Cumin, William fitzRalph, William fitzStephen 1176: William Basset, Roger fitzReinfrid 1177: Hugh de Cressy 1179: Hugh de Gaerst, Ranulf de Glanvill, Hugh Murdac 1182: William de Auberville, Osbert fitzHervey 1184: Ralph fitzStephen.[13]",
   "notes": "efn on enwiki defaults to group lower-alpha (render data-mw group=lower-alpha). Explanatory note; may contain nested refs, which are labelled separately."
  },
